5f" "basis" 1209 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030999/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030999/state.json" "file_sha256" "c2716842d162a295307704730cb6710fd5a7785273109a8f91056d11126b8d5f" "basis" 1209 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14030999/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}$ have a local maximum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d3e672e3e2faa23020a1c778d21f37b4b5a2986bc19ae090d5b92eecc72dc7" "basis" 1441 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (2x){e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}=-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=0$ is a stationary point. Next, to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =-(-1){e}^{-(-1)^{2}/2}={e}^{-1/2}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =-(1){e}^{-(1)^{2}/2}=-{e}^{-1/2}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=0$ is a local maximum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d3e672e3e2faa23020a1c778d21f37b4b5a2986bc19ae090d5b92eecc72dc7" "basis" 1441 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e6025a13f23aeb6d27243ec300cc6b7e5c4e84f091a46053ad4b987d66214240" "basis" 1441 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/state.json" "file_sha256" "f6d3e672e3e2faa23020a1c778d21f37b4b5a2986bc19ae090d5b92eecc72dc7" "basis" 1441 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040404/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-e"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer